An outdoor calisthenics set-up - pull-up and dip bars, rings, and frames for bodyweight training - would give the site something for teenagers and adults that costs nothing to use and is open all hours.

**Where we've got to**

This is at the earliest stage. Before anything can be ordered we need to work out where it would go, what a good set-up actually costs to buy and install, what safety surfacing is needed underneath, and where the money comes from.

**What would help**

If you've raised money for something like this before, know your way around a grant application, or have experience of outdoor gym equipment and what lasts, we'd love to hear from you. Equally, if you'd just use it and want to help make the case, put your hand up.

Cost to be confirmed.
